 *
 * ELF symbol-export allowlist for libzahlen_engine.so.
 *
 * Defense-in-depth alongside -fvisibility=hidden / -fvisibility-inlines-hidden
 * and -Wl,--exclude-libs,ALL: only symbols listed under `global:` enter .dynsym;
 * `local: *;` seals all internal engine/ECS/render/physics/audio symbols, private
 * member helpers of ZHLN_API classes, C++ standard-library weak instantiations,
 * and static third-party archives (Jolt, miniaudio, meshoptimizer, Clay, VMA,
 * volk, SPIRV-Reflect, GLFW, zstd).
 *
 * Portability note: entries use Itanium C++ ABI mangled prefix patterns rather
 * than `extern "C++"` demangled globs because GNU ld.bfd rejects wildcard `(*)`
 * parameter lists inside `extern "C++"`. Each non-template function matches
 * `_Z[N|NK|NO]<nested-name>[BE]*` so both plain (`E...`) and ABI-tagged
 * (`B5cxx11E...`, libc++ inline-namespace, LP64/ILP32 size_t) encodings match
 * identically across GCC, Clang, ld.bfd, ld.lld, and mold, while nested types
 * (`<digit>...`), templates (`I...`), and longer names cannot match.
 *
 * Kept strictly in bidirectional sync with ZHLN_API declarations in
 * include/Zahlen/ by configure/check_engine_exports.py (run at configure time
 * and verified against the linked DSO via `nm -D` at post-build time).
 */
